foreign  welcome to another installment of Harry  Potter Theory due to all of the demand  in the comment section today we're going  to be discussing rubius Hagrid played by  the late and great Robbie Coltrane for  those unaware Robbie Coltrane who  famously played Ruby's Hagrid and  tragically passed recently at the age of  72 Coltrane who've been fighting poor  health for the last couple of years  finally died in hospital near his home  in Scotland the last time Coltrane  appeared on camera was this year during  the 20th Harry Potter anniversary  special returned to Hogwarts and it was  here that he reassured fans that though  he may not be around forever Hagrid  isn't going anywhere forever cemented in  film and in the hearts of millions upon  millions of Hagrid fans worldwide a few  different videos were requested on The  Lovable half giant ranging from 10 best  things about Hagrid to things we don't  know about Hagrid but I decided to land  on the latter so that I can cover some  aspects of Hagrid's character that  casual fans may not have ever known  let's get into it 10. his Hogwarts house  though there has been much speculation  over the years and a considerable number  of theories it turns out that rather  unsurprisingly Hagrid was a part of  Gryffindor given Hagrid's bravery  kindness and nobility this probably  isn't much of a shock while his house is  not revealed in the books it is revealed  in an article published on Wizarding  World that makes this little factoid  Canon do you share a house with Hagrid  9. based on a real person the list of  Harry Potter characters inspired by real  people is lengthy including Severus  Snape Harry Potter Ron Weasley and even  gilderoy Lockhart to name a few so it  shouldn't come as a surprise to you that  just like these other characters Hagrid  2 was based on a real person a biker to  be precise in Harry Potter page to  screen the complete filmmaking Journey  according to Robbie Coltrane the  character was modeled on 