ng around  but quite often I found myself thinking  why are so many of these creatures  within proximity to Hogwarts yes the  Forbidden Forest is close to the school  but it's even remarked in the books that  some of these creatures are  exceptionally rare creatures like  thestrals and acromantulas as it turns  out Hagrid is the one responsible for  bringing both thestrals and acromantulas  to the UK vestrals are extremely rare  wild creatures that the ministry of  magic considers to be dangerous because  of their link to death Hagrid tamed one  male and five female thestrals to bring  to Hogwarts who spawned an entire herd  the Hogwarts thestrals are the only hand  to Ever Be Tamed and used as pants in  all of England and no other cases are  known around the world neither Hagrid is  also responsible for bringing  acromantula to England as the species is  native to Borneo Hagrid released aragog  into the forest before snagging a female  acromantula named Mosaic aragog and  mosaic's resulting colony is the only  one to exist in England 5. his weakness  given that Hagrid was the care of  magical creatures professor and showed  an affinity for magical creatures on par  with famed magic zoologist newt's  Commander you may be surprised to hear  that Hagrid's only weakness is a tiny  pet you may have heard of I can't in the  philosopher stone Hagrid tells Harry  that he don't like cats because they  make him sneeze which is why he chose to  buy Harry an owl Hedwig for his birthday  present 4. stunted magic magical powers  aren't revealed in a magical child until  they are provoked out of them sometimes  remaining dormant for a considerable  amount of time in Hagrid's case this was  the reality as his powers didn't truly  manifest until after he'd received his  Hogwarts letter and purchased his first  one from ollivanders Hagrid simply never  had an incident in his childhood where  his emotions were heightened and for  this reason his powers didn't manifest  3. he can't cast this spell in the Harry  Potter story casting the Patronus charm  seems to be a rite of passage a  signifier that to witch or wizard has  truly honed his or her magical abilities  the Patronus charm is a positive energy  force a physical representation of Hope  happiness survival and Purity it's the  primary defense that a witch or wizard  might use against Dementors as because  the Patronus does not feel despair or  hopelessness the Dementors are repelled  by its presence but what may surprise  you is that Hagrid can't cast a Patronus  in a q a with Harry Potter fans on  Twitter JK Rowling was quizzed what  Hagrid's Patronus would be in reply she  wrote Hagrid couldn't produce a Patronus  it's a very difficult spell provided  that the Patronus in corporeal form  assumes the shape of an animal Guardian  it's surprising that Hagrid doesn't have  one two where his name came from  Hagrid's full name is rubius Hagrid and  just like many of the other characters  in the story his name actually has a lot  of depth he wasn't named haphazardly  Hagrid is a big drinker who's regularly  seen by Harry to indulge in visits to  the pub and even getting inebriated his  name alludes to his personality trait  because rubius is related to the word  Ruddy which means reddish and is  apparent on someone who drinks a lot 1.  his first wand it seems strange that for  as long as we've known Hagrid he's held  an umbrella in place of a wand and while  Hagrid's original one is inside of this  umbrella it was once a fully functioning  magical item in its own right Hagrid's  first wand free umbrella was a 16-inch  Oak one rather bendy with an unknown  core material those with Oak ones  usually have an affinity with the magic  of the natural world a bendy wand  signifies a high level of adaptability  in his personality and the length of his  wand is representative of his large  stature and enormous personality and  that's it for this video thank you for  joining me in honoring the late in gr